data: {"level":2,"reviewed":{"level":2,"label":"formula / approach","text":"For the sample average, the step size on the $n$th pull is $1/n$, with $n$ counting that pull.\nSo the first pull of an action has step size one. For a constant step size, use $\\alpha$ on\nevery pull. In both cases the update is $Q \\leftarrow Q + \\text{step}\\,(r - Q)$, where $Q$ is the\nestimate for the pulled action before this pull."},"hints_note":null}

